From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: bound AP station inactivity aging

mac80211_hwsim can retain an authorized AP station after that station has
reassociated to another virtual AP.  Embedded hostapd eventually probes and
removes the stale peer, but its normal five-minute timeout is long enough to
hide the next authorization edge when a steering test returns to an AP.  The
HAL and EasyMesh agent then report contradictory owners during that interval.

Use a 30-second AP inactivity interval for HWSIM_RADIO builds.  Hostapd still
probes before removing a peer, so a legitimately associated idle station
answers and remains connected; only a station that has actually left the AP
ages out.  Physical targets retain the platform default.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal_hostapd.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_hostapd.c b/wifi_hal_hostapd.c
--- a/wifi_hal_hostapd.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_hostapd.c
@@ -219,7 +219,13 @@ void init_hostap_bss(wifi_interface_info_t *interface)
    // conf->radius->radius_max_retry_wait = RADIUS_CLIENT_MAX_WAIT;
     conf->eap_sim_db_timeout = 1;
     conf->eap_sim_id = 3;
-    conf->ap_max_inactivity = AP_MAX_INACTIVITY;
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+    /* Keep hwsim's historical AP peer rows from masking a later
+     * reassociation edge while retaining hostapd's normal liveness probe. */
+    conf->ap_max_inactivity = 30;
+#else
+    conf->ap_max_inactivity = AP_MAX_INACTIVITY;
+#endif
     conf->eapol_version = EAPOL_VERSION;
 
     conf->max_listen_interval = 65535;
